📜 Privacy Policy – QuickCode

Effective date: 28/08/2025 (last updated 30/10/2026)

QuickCode ("we", "our", or "the App") respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle your data when you use our application QuickCode – QR & Barcode Generator.

1. Information We Do Not Collect

We do not collect, store, or share any personal information that identifies you, such as your name, email or phone number.

Generating QR codes and barcodes works offline. An internet connection is used only by the advertising and analytics services described in section 4.

We do not request unnecessary permissions.

2. Information We May Collect

QuickCode may access the following only if you choose to use certain features:

Storage/Media access (optional): to save generated codes as images on your device.

Camera access (optional, only if scanning feature is added in the future): to scan QR codes or barcodes.

These permissions are used locally on your device and the App does not transfer or share any data externally.

3. How We Use Data

All generated codes (QR, Barcode, etc.) are created and processed locally on your device.

We do not send, upload, or store your codes on external servers.

Your data stays 100% private.

4. Third-Party Services

QuickCode shows ads through Google AdMob and uses Firebase Analytics (both from Google). Their data processing is described in the section "Data processed by third-party SDKs" below. If in the future we include other third-party services, this Privacy Policy will be updated accordingly.

5. Data Security

We are committed to keeping your information safe:

No external storage of personal data.

No collection of the codes you generate.

Data processed by third-party SDKs (as declared in Google Play Data safety)

This section lists, for QuickCode, the data processed by the third-party SDKs included in the app. It matches the Data safety form of the app on Google Play.

- Google AdMob (advertising): collects and shares with Google the advertising ID / app set ID and other device identifiers, an approximate location derived from your IP address, ad interactions (impressions, clicks) and diagnostics (such as app launches and performance). Purposes: advertising, ad measurement and analytics, and fraud prevention and security. We do not receive your name or contact details from AdMob.
- Firebase Analytics (Google): app interactions (events and screens viewed), the Firebase installation ID / device identifiers, and basic device and app information. Purposes: analytics and app functionality.

Ad choices: you can reset or delete your advertising ID and opt out of ads personalisation in Android Settings > Google > Ads.
Security: data sent to these services travels encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS).
Data deletion: the app has no user accounts. Data stored on your device is deleted by uninstalling the app or clearing its data; for data held by Google (advertising ID, analytics), reset your advertising ID as described above or write to tll.developers.apps@gmail.com and we will help with the request.

6. Children’s Privacy

QuickCode can be used by children with supervision. However, we recommend supervision if used in educational environments.

7. Changes to This Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be published in this section, and the effective date will be updated.

8. Contact Us

If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, you can contact us at:

